missed.claim:
Grothendieck links three things explicitly:
- the elliptic-point (2- and 3-cycle) relations of the Galois action on π_{0,3}^;
- Galois representations on Tate modules of the CM curves at λ = 1/2 and λ = −j;
- the level-2 lifting to M_{1,1}[2] ⊂ T_{1,1}, which carries a quadratic-twist ambiguity.
The ingredients exist separately (Anderson/Ihara Jacobi-sum formulae, Nakamura's genus-one work). However, an explicit statement that the elliptic GT relations encode the CM Hecke characters of j = 0 and j = 1728, up to a twist fixed by the Legendre lift, is not standard.
